=EF=BB=BFI'm forced to using external tools in some recipes (that build FPG=
A bitstreams=20
using huge proprietary packages). Building these takes between half an hour=
=20
and several hours on big fast machines, so I definitely want to use=20
sstate-cache for these.

The trouble I'm running into is that I have a variable like XILINX_TOOL_PAT=
H=20
which is in local.conf so people can tell where the tools are.

The compile part of the recipe runs something like=20
${XILINX_TOOL_PATH}/bin/something

This makes the "compile" step dependent on that variable. When a machine=20
installs the tools somewhere else, it will have a different value for that=
=20
tool, and because OE thinks that matters, it will insist on building its ve=
ry=20
own version of that package instead of just fetching it from the sstate-cac=
he=20
on the buildserver.

How do I explain to OE that the value of this variable does not matter for =
the=20
sstate-cache?

I tried: do_compile[vardepsexclude] =3D "XILINX_TOOL_PATH"

that didn't appear to help.


